Z||000000||rigdonhome||11-04-2001||07:01 PM||||I'm swapping my V8 into a different S10 body soon, and this new body has a factory tach that I would like to keep.  Of course, the S10 never came with a V8, so some kind of recalibration will be necessary.<P>I know you V8 Fiero guys have ALL done this...  How do you do it?  Does someone sell a 'whatzit' that I can just plug in?<P>Cheers,<BR>Scott<P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black, 5-speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Web Site:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/</A> <BR>Story of buying my Fiero:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/rear_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||4
